  "math_boundaries": [
    "FP8 BF16 dynamic PowerOfTwo profile uses the actual original encoded E4 weights and exact original scale widening; encoded-A MatMul independently yields F32 output. Both CPU and CUDA use the same explicit boundaries.",
    "Qwen6/15 actual code*BF16SF has11226/4479 non-BF16 products; each F32 projection profile distinguishes8/9 outputs from an incorrect early BF16 weight product. This proves the candidate public arithmetic, not the publisher chosen activation/weight-product policy.",
    "DeepSeek25/26 I8 is retained bit-for-bit as adjacent two-nibble E2M1, with original E8M0 group32 widened exactly to F32; GroupedFloat4Linear executes dynamic group128 E4 activation and F32 dot/scale blocks. Omitting activation quantization changes6/18 and2/18 outputs respectively per backend.",
    "Inferact19 follows the fixed vLLM reader: numeric F32->E8M0 RNE then BF16 unchanged activation. This selected tile has192 exact power2 scales, so it does not witness non-power2 import thresholds; existing independent generic import tests cover those boundaries. Wrongly inserting activation quantization changes6/18 outputs per backend.",
    "Atlas27 original F32SF values in this tile happen to be exact2^-10; they are copied unchanged, never assumed/re-encoded from the quantization label."
  ],
  "product_fix": {
    "problem": "CUDA grouped FP4 admission hardcoded four whole-model(N,K) shapes, even though its actual kernel masks arbitrary final N64 load/store tiles.",
    "change": "Replace the four-shape whitelist with actual signedI32 argument/A-quantizer bounds, z-grid token-slot cap and PTRDIFF address extents. Keep public positive/K%128 format validation, real resource permissions/alignment and original numeric kernel unchanged.",
    "width_proof": "Kernel weight/scale/output pointer products and N/K loop indices are unsigned64. The original activation quantizer is signedI32, so (tokens*activation_slots)*K<=INT32_MAX is checked by division before multiplication; tokens*slots<=65535. Every admitted ABI field is <=INT32_MAX. Public encoded descriptors prove checked physical extents, additionally <=PTRDIFF_MAX.",
    "regression": "Actual N3/K128, odd65/K256,129/K384, old4096/K2048; shared/per-slot A and duplicate IDs. OversizeN/K/E, token/slot z-grid, flattenedA I32 overflow and host-resource negatives. Existing actual-down cancellation F32 precision remains passing."
  },
  "limits": [
    "CUDA dynamic Float8BlockLinear PowerOfTwo currently genuinely declines F32 A; the F32 test explicitly supplies already encoded A to ordinary MatMul rather than claiming that dynamic variant.",
    "BF16-scale Qwen6/15 producer/reader activation and weight rounding are still a source-binding decision. Lossless scale representation does not prove complete source arithmetic.",
    "Original Inferact exporter/OAS equivalence, other undeclared hardware FP4 reductions, complete trained routing/state, full models, quality and throughput are not claimed.",
    "The source expert tile is an explicitly supplied component ID0; no model router is claimed to select it. Original complete experts were not downloaded."
  ],
